The Go module and build scripts are original code under LICENSE (MIT).

The SQLite engine is compiled, without source modifications, from the official
SQLite amalgamation. SQLite deliverable code is public domain:
https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html
Source URL, SHA-256, official SHA3-256, compiler and flags accompany every asset.

Linux and Windows assets are compiled with Zig/LLVM. Relevant compiler/runtime,
MinGW-w64 and glibc notices are provided under third_party/. The SQLite libraries
link against the target platform's libc/system libraries; those platform libraries
are not embedded in this module. Toolchain distributions and runtime source are
available from the pinned upstream URLs in scripts/install-zig.py and Zig 0.17.0:
https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.0/zig-0.17.0.tar.xz
https://github.com/ziglang/zig/tree/0.17.0/lib
